---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="35–45 min" data-extension-duration="10–15 min">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>The verb <em>to be</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">The most common verb in English. We use <span class="ex">to be</span> to talk about who we are, how we feel, our age, and where things are.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 35–45 min</span>
    <span class="tag">am / is / are</span>
    <span class="tag">Present simple</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>See how be links two ideas.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Learn</b><span>Choose am, is, or are.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Practice</b><span>Build sentences and questions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Speak</b><span>Talk about yourself and your class.</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h2>By the end of this lesson, you can…</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>say who you are: <span class="ex">I am Ana. My name is Ana.</span></li>
      <li>choose <span class="ex">am</span>, <span class="ex">is</span>, or <span class="ex">are</span> for any subject.</li>
      <li>ask and answer simple questions: <span class="ex">Are you a student? Yes, I am.</span></li>
      <li>make a sentence negative: <span class="ex">I am not tired.</span></li>
      <li>use short forms when you speak: <span class="ex">I’m · you’re · she’s.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice first</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Think it through</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">I am Ana. &nbsp; My name is Ana. &nbsp; We are students.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which word changes after <strong>I</strong>, <strong>name</strong>, and <strong>we</strong>?</li>
      <li>Are these sentences actions, or are they descriptions?</li>
      <li>What is the word <strong>be</strong> connecting?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What does <em>be</em> mean?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Many common verbs describe <strong>actions</strong>, such as <span class="ex">run, eat, study</span>. The verb <strong>to be</strong> is different. It connects a person or thing to information about identity, description, feeling, age, or location.</p>
  <p>Think of <strong>be</strong> as an equals sign <strong>(=)</strong>:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">I <strong>am</strong> Ana.</span> → I = Ana. &nbsp; <span class="ex">She <strong>is</strong> happy.</span> → she = happy. &nbsp; <span class="ex">They <strong>are</strong> at work.</span> → they = at work.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Try this</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Point as you say it: <strong>I</strong> (point to yourself), <strong>you</strong> (point to the other person), <strong>they</strong> (point to two people).</li>
      <li>Say the whole piece, not one word at a time: <span class="ex">I am</span>, <span class="ex">he is</span>, <span class="ex">we are</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>The forms</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Full form</th><th>Contraction</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>I</td><td><b>am</b></td><td class="contraction">I’m</td></tr>
      <tr><td>You</td><td><b>are</b></td><td class="contraction">you’re</td></tr>
      <tr><td>He / She / It</td><td><b>is</b></td><td class="contraction">he’s / she’s / it’s</td></tr>
      <tr><td>We</td><td><b>are</b></td><td class="contraction">we’re</td></tr>
      <tr><td>They</td><td><b>are</b></td><td class="contraction">they’re</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Learn these as whole pieces: <span class="ex">I am</span>, <span class="ex">you are</span>, <span class="ex">she is</span>. Don’t build them word by word. Say the whole piece.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. My name and he use is; we and they use are.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the form</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Tap a gap, then choose the word</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Hello, my name <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="My name refers to one name, so use is." data-fix="Use is: My name is Ana." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Ana.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="Use are after we." data-fix="Use are: We are from Brazil." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from Brazil.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="Use is after he." data-fix="Use is: He is not at home." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> not at home. He’s at work.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="Use are after they." data-fix="Use are: They are my friends." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my friends.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. A question with you begins with Are, and the positive short answer is Yes, I am.">
    <h3>Drill 1B: ask and answer</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Choose the complete question and short-answer forms.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Are">Are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Is">Is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Are" data-hint="The subject is you. Put the matching form of be before it." data-fix="Ask: Are you a teacher?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> you a teacher?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Yes, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-hint="The subject in the answer is I." data-fix="Answer: Yes, I am." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. Use am with I, is with she and my name, and are with you and they.">
    <h3>Drill 2: match the subject</h3>
    <p>Tap a subject tile, then tap the matching be form.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="am">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="is">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="are">You</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="is">My name</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="are">They</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="am" data-hint="Use am only with I." data-fix="Match I with am." data-placeholder="am">am</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="is" data-hint="Choose a singular subject that uses is." data-fix="Match an is subject: She or My name." data-placeholder="is">is</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="are" data-hint="Choose a subject that uses are." data-fix="Match an are subject: You or They." data-placeholder="are">are</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="is" data-hint="Choose the other singular subject that uses is." data-fix="Match the remaining is subject: She or My name." data-placeholder="is">is</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="are" data-hint="Choose the other subject that uses are." data-fix="Match the remaining are subject: You or They." data-placeholder="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Say it short</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In everyday speech, we often join the subject and <strong>be</strong> in a <strong>short form</strong>, also called a contraction. Contractions are neutral and very common. Full forms are also correct and are useful when you want to speak clearly or add emphasis.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Full form</th><th>Short form</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>I am</td><td><b>I’m</b></td><td class="ex">I’m a student.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>you are</td><td><b>you’re</b></td><td class="ex">You’re right.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>he is</td><td><b>he’s</b></td><td class="ex">He’s at home.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>she is</td><td><b>she’s</b></td><td class="ex">She’s happy.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>they are</td><td><b>they’re</b></td><td class="ex">They’re my friends.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: make <em>be</em> small and the new information clear</h3>
    <p>Say the subject and short form together. Then give the strongest beat to the important new word.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>sentence</th><th>natural rhythm</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>I’m a student.</td><td>I’m a <b>STU</b>dent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>She’s happy.</td><td>She’s <b>HAP</b>py.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>They’re at work.</td><td>They’re at <b>WORK</b>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>In speech, the words can link in <span class="ex">Are you ready?</span> and <span class="ex">Is she at home?</span>, but they remain separate words in writing. In a positive short answer, keep the full verb: <span class="ex">Yes, I am</span> and <span class="ex">Yes, she is</span>, not <span class="ex">Yes, I’m</span> or <span class="ex">Yes, she’s</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Speak: say it short</h3>
    <p>Read the full sentence, say the short form out loud, then tap to check. Say each one quickly, like one word.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I am from Spain. → short</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’m</strong> from Spain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> You are very kind. → short</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You’re</strong> very kind.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> He is my brother. → short</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He’s</strong> my brother.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> She is a doctor. → short</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She’s</strong> a doctor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> They are at school. → short</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They’re</strong> at school.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Negatives and questions</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><strong>Negative:</strong> add <span class="ex">not</span> after <strong>be</strong>: <span class="ex">I am not</span>, <span class="ex">she is not</span>, <span class="ex">they are not</span>.</p>
  <p>Common negative contractions are <span class="ex">isn’t</span> and <span class="ex">aren’t</span>. With <span class="ex">I</span>, say <span class="ex">I’m not</span>, not <span class="ex">I amn’t</span>.</p>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> move <strong>be</strong> before the subject: <span class="ex">Are you a student?</span> <span class="ex">Is she from Spain?</span> <span class="ex">Am I late?</span></p>
  <p><strong>Good news:</strong> with <strong>be</strong>, you do not need <span class="ex">do</span>. Say <span class="ex">Are you a student?</span>, never <span class="ex">Do you are…?</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Watch out: common beginner mistakes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="cross">✗</span> <s>I have 20 years.</s> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">I am 20 (years old).</span></li>
      <li><span class="cross">✗</span> <s>She happy.</s> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">She is happy.</span> (do not drop <em>be</em>)</li>
      <li><span class="cross">✗</span> <s>Do you are a student?</s> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">Are you a student?</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="are you a student" data-hint="A question with be begins with Are, followed by the subject you." data-fix="Build: Are you a student?" data-success-message="Correct. In a question with be, Are comes before the subject you.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap the words in order. Then ask the question aloud.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="student">student</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">Are</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap tiles here"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="do" data-hint="A question with be does not need an extra helper verb." data-fix="Are you a student?" data-why="With the verb to be, put be before the subject. Do not use do.">
    <h3>Drill 4: spot the error</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that makes this question wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">Do</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="student">a student?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 5: say it, then check</h3>
    <p>Say your answer out loud first. Then tap to check.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> You are happy. → question</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Are you</strong> happy?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> She is at home. → negative</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer>She <strong>is not</strong> at home.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> They are friends. → question</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Are they</strong> friends?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Speak: make it real</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Make it true for you:</b> finish each sentence so it is true about <strong>you</strong>. Say it out loud, then write it.
    <br /><span class="ex">My name is ____.</span>
    <br /><span class="ex">I am from ____.</span>
    <br /><span class="ex">I am a ____.</span> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(your job, or “student”)</span>
    <br /><span class="ex">I am ____ years old.</span>
    <br /><span class="ex">Today I am ____.</span> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(happy · tired · fine · busy)</span>
  </div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Mini interview:</b> ask a partner, then answer with a short form. <span class="ex">Are you from Mexico?</span> <span class="ex">Are you a teacher?</span> <span class="ex">Are you tired today?</span> Short answers: <span class="ex">Yes, I am.</span> / <span class="ex">No, I’m not.</span></div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-lesson-extension="Extra class-profile agreement practice" data-success-message="Great. Use is with Sara and she, are with Tom and Lily and they, am with I, and are with you.">
    <h3>Meet the class: choose the correct sentence</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She is a teacher." data-hint="Sara is one woman, so the subject is she." data-fix="Use is with she: She is a teacher.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Sara: from Italy; a teacher</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She is a teacher.">She is a teacher.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She are a teacher.">She are a teacher.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She am a teacher.">She am a teacher.</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="They are students." data-hint="Tom and Lily are two people, so the subject is they." data-fix="Use are with they: They are students.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Tom and Lily: from the USA; students</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They is students.">They is students.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They are students.">They are students.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They am students.">They am students.</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I am a doctor." data-hint="The profile says Me, so speak with I." data-fix="Use am with I: I am a doctor.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Me: my name is Leo; a doctor</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I is a doctor.">I is a doctor.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I are a doctor.">I are a doctor.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I am a doctor.">I am a doctor.</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="You are very kind." data-hint="Use are with the subject you." data-fix="The correct sentence is: You are very kind.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. You: very kind</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You is very kind.">You is very kind.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You am very kind.">You am very kind.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You are very kind.">You are very kind.</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. The subject chooses am, is, or are; questions move be first, and negatives put not after be.">
    <h3>Final quiz: can you use <em>be</em>?</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is" data-hint="My name refers to one name, so use is." data-fix="Use is: My name is Ana.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. My name ___ Ana.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am">am</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="are" data-hint="The subject is you. Put the matching form of be before it." data-fix="Ask: Are you from Brazil?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. ___ you from Brazil?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am" data-value-label-variant="case">Am</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is" data-value-label-variant="case">Is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are" data-value-label-variant="case">Are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She is not at home." data-hint="With be, put not after is. Do not add do." data-fix="The correct negative is: She is not at home.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Sara is at work now. Which negative sentence about home is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She is not at home.">She is not at home.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She not is at home.">She not is at home.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She does not at home.">She does not at home.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="am" data-hint="The short answer has the subject I." data-fix="Answer: Yes, I am.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Are you ready? Yes, I ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am">am</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="are" data-hint="Use are after they." data-fix="Use are: They are my friends.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. They ___ my friends.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am">am</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Choose the form by meaning</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Say one true sentence about yourself with <span class="ex">I am</span>.</li>
      <li>Say one true sentence about another person with <span class="ex">he is</span> or <span class="ex">she is</span>.</li>
      <li>Say one true sentence about two people with <span class="ex">they are</span>.</li>
      <li>Turn one of your statements into a question.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> At the start of the next lesson, open the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute retrieval</a>. Then introduce yourself and one person you know in three sentences and ask your teacher one <span class="ex">Are you…?</span> question.</div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day retrieval">
    <h2>Come back tomorrow: five-minute retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Do not read the forms table first. Answer from memory, check, and then say each complete sentence aloud.</p>

    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Good retrieval. Use am with I, is with my teacher, and Are before you in a question.">
      <h3>Three choices from memory</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Are">Are</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-hint="Use am with I." data-fix="Say: I am from Mexico." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from Mexico.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My teacher <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="My teacher is one person, like he or she." data-fix="Say: My teacher is from the United States." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from the United States.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Are" data-hint="Put the form of be for you before the subject." data-fix="Ask: Are you tired today?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> you tired today?</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions">
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="do" data-hint="A question with be does not use do." data-fix="Are you at home?" data-why="Put Are before you. Do not use do with the verb be.">
      <h3>One repair from memory</h3>
      <p>Tap the extra word in this question.</p>
      <div class="spot-options">
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">Do</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="home">at home?</button>
      </div>
      <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Two no-notes recall prompts</h3>
      <p>Say the complete answer before you reveal it.</p>
      <div class="transform-list">
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Complete the three pairs: I ___; she ___; we ___.</p>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
          <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I am; she is; we are.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Change “You are ready” to a question.</p>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
          <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Are you ready?</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prompt-card"><b>Speak for 30 seconds:</b> Say your name, where you are from, and how you feel today. Then ask one <span class="ex">Are you…?</span> question.</div>
  </section>
</main>
